    "title": "Definition of T cell - NCI Dictionary of Cancer Terms - NCI",
    "text": "Skip to main content T cellListen to pronunciation(... sel)A type of white blood cell. T cells are part of the immune system and develop from stem cells in the bone marrow. They help protect the body from infection and may help fight cancer. Also called T lymphocyte and thymocyte.Enlarge this image in new windowBlood cell development. A blood stem cell goes through several steps to become a red blood cell, platelet, or white blood cell. Search NCI's Dictionary of Cancer TermsStarts withContains",
